# The world around: weather, seasons, the stars, old stories everyone knows; and the land itself (doc 60): Ridgemere,
# the only city, on its hills above the Sound; the six towns; the Long River; the snowy north-east and the warm south.

scene wt2_rain_work
when topic=weather here.weather=rain|storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a[merchant] : Nobody shops in the rain. | My awning's leaking onto the goods.
a[laborer] : Hauling in the rain. Twice the weight, half the pay.
a : Rain, rain, rain. | Everything's mud. | Can't get dry.
b[old] : Rain's good for the wells. Be grateful.
b[child] : I like the rain! Splash!
b : It'll pass. | Mud everywhere. | #bc_nor_me#
a : Eventually. | Everywhere. | #bc_never#

scene wt2_storm_fear
when topic=weather here.weather=storm
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Hear that thunder? | Lightning struck the old oak last storm. | My shutters nearly blew off.
b[child] : I'm not scared. I'm not! Is it over yet?
b[old] : The sky's angry. It'll calm.
b : Stay inside. | Split it clean, didn't it? | Nail them shut.
a : #bc_i_will# | Clean in two. | I did.

scene wt2_fog_creepy
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Fog like this, anything could be out there. | Can't see the end of my nose. | The fog's swallowed the whole street.
b[guard] : Thieves love a fog.
b[old] : Fog's just a cloud that got tired.
b : Don't say that. | Stay close. | It'll lift.
a : #bc_sorry# | #bc_i_will# | #bc_hope_so#

scene wt2_snow_beauty
when topic=weather here.weather=snow
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Look how quiet the snow makes everything. | First snow's always the prettiest. | Everything looks clean under snow.
b[child] : Can we make snow wolves?
b[old] : Pretty till you have to walk in it.
b : #bc_it_does# | Until it's grey slush. | For a day.
a : #bc_lovely# | #bc_true# | For a day.

scene wt2_overcast
when topic=weather here.weather=overcast
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Grey all day. | Sun hasn't shown its face in days. | Looks like rain, doesn't it?
b : Might. | Gloomy. | Always looks like rain.
a : Might not. | #bc_very# | #bc_ha#

scene wt2_season_change_spring
when topic=smalltalk|weather here.season=spring
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : Mud season. | The thaw's flooded the low lanes. | Lambs in the fields already.
b[farmer] : Busiest time of year.
b : #bc_always_is# | #bc_every_year# | Spring's here.
a : #bc_always# | #bc_every_year# | At last.

scene wt2_season_change_autumn
when topic=smalltalk|weather here.season=autumn
does tell.self / react.self / assess
a : The geese are flying south. | First frost this morning. | Gathering season.
b[old] : Early geese, hard winter.
b : Already? | Cold one. | Busy time.
a : #bc_already# | #bc_very# | #bc_very#

scene lr_stars
when topic=lore here.time=night|dusk
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : See the Wolf in the stars, there? | The Hunter's rising early this year. | My father named every star.
b[old] : My mother told me the stars are the ancestors watching.
b[child] : Where? Show me!
b : I see it. | Early winter, then. | Do you remember them?
a : Beautiful. | #bc_so_they_say# | Some.

scene lr_moon
when topic=lore here.time=night
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : Big moon tonight. | They say a full moon makes pups wild. | Moon's red tonight. Bad sign.
b[old] : The moon was bigger when I was young. Or I was smaller.
b[child] : I feel wild! Awooo!
b : #bc_lovely# | Makes everyone wild. | Just dust in the air.
a : #bc_very# | #bc_ha# | #bc_maybe#

scene lr_first_wolves
when topic=lore
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : They say the first wolves walked out of the mountain. | My grandmother said we came from across the sea. | Do you believe the old stories?
b[priest] : The old stories hold truth, if not facts.
b[old] : I believe the stories that keep pups behaving.
b : Every town has its own story. | Mine says something else. | Some of them.
a : #bc_true# | Everyone's does. | Some.

scene lr_ghosts
when topic=lore
does tell.story / react.story / assess
weight 0.7
a : Do you believe in ghosts? | My house creaks at night like someone's walking. | I saw something in the old well once.
b[old] : I've seen three. Two were drunk. One wasn't.
b[priest] : The dead rest. Mostly.
b[child] : Ghosts aren't real. Are they?
b : No. | Old houses creak. | What was it?
a : Nor me. Mostly. | I suppose. | I never found out.

scene lr_dragons
when topic=lore
does tell.story / react.story / assess
weight 0.5
a : My uncle swears he saw a great serpent in the hills. | There are bones in the hills bigger than houses. | Monsters lived here once.
b[scholar] : The bones are old. Very old. Not monsters.
b : Your uncle drinks. | Have you seen them? | And now there's us.
a : He does. | Once. | #bc_ha#

scene lr_proverbs
when topic=lore|smalltalk
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : Like my mother always said: a full belly forgives everything. | A wolf alone is a wolf in danger. | Never trust a fox who smiles.
b[old] : She was a wise wolf, your mother.
b : #bc_true_enough# | Very true. | Nor a merchant.
a : She was. | #bc_it_is# | #bc_ha#

scene lr_old_war
when topic=lore
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : My grandfather fought in the old war. | There's a battlefield past the hills, still full of rusted blades. | Nobody remembers what the war was about.
b[old] : I remember. Barely. Everyone was hungry.
b[soldier] : Wars are always about the same thing. Somebody wanted more.
b : Was he brave? | I'd not go there. | Nobody ever does.
a : He said not. | #bc_nor_me# | #bc_never#

scene lr_harvest_moon
when topic=lore here.season=autumn
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : Harvest moon soon. | They say if you wish on the harvest moon, it comes true. | The old ones danced in the fields under the harvest moon.
b[farmer] : I'll be too tired to dance.
b : Make a wish, then. | Did it ever work? | Nobody dances now.
a : #bc_i_will# | Sometimes. | More's the pity.

scene lr_winter_tale
when topic=lore here.season=winter
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : They say in the hardest winter, the river froze to the bottom. | A winter so cold birds fell from the sky. | My grandmother survived the Long Winter.
b[old] : I remember the Long Winter. We ate bark.
b[child] : Will this winter be long?
b : Hard to believe. | Terrible. | How?
a : It's true. | #bc_very# | She never said.

scene lr_luck
when topic=lore|smalltalk
does tell.story / react.story / assess
weight 0.6
a : Found a white stone today. Good luck. | Saw a heron. That's luck, isn't it? | My lucky charm's gone. Lost it.
b[old] : Luck's what you make. And a white stone helps.
b : #bc_lucky_you# | Herons are luck. | Find another.
a : #bc_hope_so# | #bc_good# | #bc_ill_try#

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- The land (doc 60)

scene wt3_the_city_from_afar
when topic=lore|smalltalk here.region=towns
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : My cousin went to Ridgemere. Says it rained every day. | Have you ever seen Ridgemere? The only real city there is. | They say Ridgemere's built on hills, one street on top of the next.
b[merchant] : Ridgemere pays well for what we send. I'd go myself if the road were shorter.
b : Every day? | Never. Too far. | Sounds like a lot of stairs.
a : Every single one. | One day, maybe. | And all of them wet.

scene wt3_the_towns_from_the_city
when topic=lore|smalltalk here.region=ridgemere
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : Six towns out there, and not one bigger than the Sump. | My mother was from Southmeadow. Said the sun shone there. | They say up in Frosthollow the snow never leaves.
b[carter] : I've driven to every one. The South Road's mud, and the High Road's worse.
b : And twice as dry. | The sun! Imagine. | Not even in summer?
a : Dry sounds nice. | I try to. | Not even then.

scene wt3_long_river
when topic=lore|smalltalk here.region=lake|countryside here.region!=waste
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : The Long River starts in Glasswater, they say, and ends in the Drowned Delta. | My father took a raft down the Long River once. Halfway, anyway. | Half the south drinks from the Long River.
b[old] : That river was here before any of us. It'll be here after.
b : That's a long way. | Only halfway? | The thirsty half.
a : It's in the name. | The fens stopped him. | Which is all of it, in summer.

scene wt3_north_and_south
when topic=lore|smalltalk
does tell.story / react.story / assess
weight 0.7
a : North-east it's all mountains and snow, they say. | Down in the south-west the woods are warm even in winter. | The Sunfields grow half the bread we eat.
b[old] : Snow one end, swamp the other, and rain on Ridgemere. That's the whole world.
b : I'll take your word for it. | Warm in winter? | And the rest?
a : #bc_wise# | #bc_so_they_say# | Rabbit, mostly.

scene wt3_whitefangs
when topic=lore|weather here.region=mountains
does tell.story / react.story / assess
a : The Whitefangs are clear today. You can count the peaks. | Snow's come down off the Whitefangs early. | The pass up to Frosthollow is closed again.
b[miner] : Mountains give the ore and take the miners. Fair trade, some say.
b : I make it eleven. | It always does. | Wait it out.
a : There's more behind. | Early and hard. | Nothing else to do.
